        "content": "<p>wraitii edited <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15201\">PR #15201</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The elaborator’s loop stack can include a loop that dominates the current block but has already exited. Treating the stack as a nested loop chain can hoist instructions across that unrelated loop, extending live ranges without reducing repeated work.</p>\n<p>Pseudocode example of the issue:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">hot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n<span class=\"kr\">do</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nc\">hot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">random</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">0.5</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">// Un-necessary but this shows that hoisting before is generally incorrect.</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">return</span>\n<span class=\"k\">while</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">!=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">cold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n<span class=\"kr\">do</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nc\">step</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">unsigned</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">63</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">cold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">step</span>\n<span class=\"k\">while</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">!=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Incorrect placement before the fix:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">step</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">unsigned</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">63</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">// hoisted across the unrelated hot loop</span>\n<span class=\"n\">hot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n<span class=\"kr\">do</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nc\">hot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">random</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">0.5</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"nc\">return</span>\n<span class=\"k\">while</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">!=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">cold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n<span class=\"kr\">do</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nc\">cold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">step</span>\n<span class=\"k\">while</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">!=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The fix places step after the hot loop, before the cold loop. The code remains correct in both cases but the generation is significantly worse, especially as this increases register pressure.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>PR written by Astra, the diff reads correct to me for the issue but i've been peepholing these, so feel free to pong back.</p>\n</blockquote>",
